   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "At x = 5 the numerator is sqrt(9) - 3 = 0 and the denominator is 0, so the form is zero over zero.",
         "mathjson": 0
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Multiply numerator and denominator by the conjugate sqrt(x + 4) + 3. The numerator becomes (x + 4) - 9 = x - 5, so the quotient is (x - 5)/((x - 5)(sqrt(x + 4) + 3)).",
         "mathjson": [
